# Syntax cheat sheet

The tags you will use most. Every example here is drawn live by Keydown!

## Lines

Start a line with one of these and a space:

| Write | You get |
| --- | --- |
| `# Heading` ... `###### Heading` | Heading levels 1 to 6 |
| `#= Heading` | The extra large **mega header** |
| `* item` | A bullet point |
| `> text` | A quote |
| `-# text` | **Subtext**: small, dim text for notes |
| `::pagebreak` | A new page |

-# This line is subtext, drawn by `-# text`!

## Inline

| Write | You get |
| --- | --- |
| `**bold**` | **bold** |
| `*italic*` | *italic* |
| Backticks around a word | `code` |
| `[link](https://radii-office.com)` | [link](https://radii-office.com) |
| `{key Ctrl+K}` | {key Ctrl+K} |

## Chips

* `++R+glossy++` gives ++R+glossy++ (a glossy Aero chip)!
* `#G#a green chip#` gives #G#a green chip#!
* `=B=orb=B=` gives =B=orb=B=, a gel orb!
* `{badge New}` gives {badge New}, a small badge (add a color after a bar, like `{badge New` then a bar then `green}`)!
* `{chip teal ticket}ADMIT ONE{/chip}` gives {chip teal ticket}ADMIT ONE{/chip}!

The letters pick the color. R is red, G is green, B is blue, and many more exist (see the reference)!

## Writing a symbol as itself

If you want to show a tag instead of using it, put a backslash before the symbols, like `\#R\#not a chip\#`. Words that only look like Keydown, such as AT&T and R&D, stay as typed!

## Math

`$E = mc^2$` gives $E = mc^2$, and a line with `$$ ... $$` gives a larger centered equation!

## Callouts

```
::note Your own title
Text inside the box.
::end
```

::note Your own title
Text inside the box. There are also tip, info, warning, danger, success and important!
::end

